COUNTEREXAMPLE_J1_1 D(x)={1/x} for x>0,{0} otherwise: closed graph/compact convex values and graph-bounded affine f=-2+xd, but Psi(x)={-1} for x>0 and {-2} at x=0; Psi not usc. This refutes the cited proof, not existence in every such model.
COUNTEREXAMPLE_POST_CLOSURE xdot=d in {+/-1}, zdot=x^2, initial (0,0): time-1 points (0,1/(12N^2)) approach unattainable (0,0); compact action values do not ensure closed ordinary reach.
COUNTEREXAMPLE_R3 rho=1, h=id: B={(-1,0),(1,0)} has two-point midpoint cell; B_N={(-1,0),(1+1/N,0)} has only singleton cells, so the two-point posterior cannot be approximated.
SENSOR_SCOPE exact y=1[x>=0] has a half-open negative cell; allowing both readings at 0 is a different, multivalued tie convention.
CHECK_INFORMATION_ORDER g=ud-1/2: policy seeing d=+/-1 can choose u=d and avoid negative drift, although a uniform d*=0 defeats all u; pointwise quantifier order must be typed.
